 deepfake:{scene:'Frame observatory',problem:'A manipulated video can look plausible frame by frame. Video-level classification needs a consistent preprocessing and aggregation path.',contribution:'An OpenCV preprocessing pipeline and MobileNetV2 transfer-learning workflow for authentic-versus-manipulated video classification.',decision:'Sample eight frames, use a detected face when available, resize to 128 × 128, then aggregate the three largest frame scores.',outcome:'The repository contains training and prediction scripts. The cinematic walkthrough executes the same top-three aggregation rule on clearly labeled example scores.',scope:'The trained model weights are absent from the public repository. This portfolio does not claim live deepfake inference or a measured accuracy.',evidence:[]},
