 'playable-replay':{scene:'Reconstruction arcade',problem:'Watching a recording and playing a reconstructed game are different tasks. Takeover requires an explicit state and a model that can continue without future ball positions.',contribution:'A seven-stage pipeline from capture and tracking through contact extraction, physics fitting, reconstruction, takeover and verification.',decision:'Fit on the chronological first 60% of observations. For continuous replay, start from one observed seed and recorded paddle controls; do not resynchronize future ball states.',outcome:'The scene uses the actual exported Staggered reconstruction and original engine. A reliable observed frame can become a new player-controlled branch.',scope:'The source clip is a synthetic fixture. Uploaded-video reconstruction supports a bounded fixed-camera Breakout family; real-game generalization remains unvalidated.',evidence:[{type:'video',src:'assets/evidence/replay-source.webm',poster:'apps/playable-replay/frames/000000.png',alt:'Source footage of the synthetic Staggered Breakout fixture.',caption:'Original source clip for the Staggered synthetic fixture. Compare the recording with the inferred model, then take over a reliable frame in the real demo.'}]},
